 "sentences": [
  {
   "text": "Pablo Escobar's hippos are still alive, and Colombia has approved killing them.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 5.04
  },
  {
   "text": "In 1981, he imported four of them for his private zoo.",
   "start": 5.6,
   "end": 9.0
  },
  {
   "text": "His estate lay between Medell\u00edn and Bogot\u00e1.",
   "start": 9.72,
   "end": 12.0
  },
  {
   "text": "After he died in 1993, they escaped and spread.",
   "start": 12.48,
   "end": 15.66
  },
  {
   "text": "By 2007 there were sixteen, by 2014 about forty, and now around two hundred.",
   "start": 16.26,
   "end": 22.087
  },
  {
   "text": "In April 2026, Colombia approved killing more than eighty of them.",
   "start": 22.56,
   "end": 26.46
  },
  {
   "text": "An Indian billionaire offered to take them to India instead.",
   "start": 26.46,
   "end": 29.66
  },
  {
   "text": "Conservationists call them invasive; some ecologists disagree.",
   "start": 30.8,
   "end": 33.98
  },
  {
   "text": "So who decides their fate?",
   "start": 34.86,
   "end": 36.3
  }
 ]
